ons are \n\n$$\n{y}_{1}(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x\\sqrt{\\lambda }),\\,{y}_{2}(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x\\sqrt{\\lambda })\n$$\n\nand the general solution is\n\n$$\ny=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x\\sqrt{\\lambda })+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x\\sqrt{\\lambda }).\n$$\n\nApplying the boundary condition $y(0)=0$ yields\n\n$$\nA\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)=0\n$$\n\nwhich gives $A=0.$ So, we have\n\n$$\ny=B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x\\sqrt{\\lambda }).\n$$\n\nApplying the boundary condition $y(\\pi )=0$ yields\n\n$$\nB\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\pi \\sqrt{\\lambda })=0.\n$$\n\nFor nontrivial solutions, we require \n\n$$\n4\\pi \\sqrt{\\lambda }=n\\pi \n$$\n\nfor $n\\in N.$ This gives the parameter values corresponding to the eigenvalues:\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{n}=\\frac{{n}^{2}}{16}.\n$$\n\nThe corresponding eigenfunctions are \n\n$$\n{y}_{n}(x)={B}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{n}}),\\,{B}_{n}\\in R.\n$$" 13194139535924 true] [17592186374667 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374668 13194139535924 true] [17592186374667 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374669 13194139535924 true] [17592186374667 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374670 13194139535924 true] [17592186374667 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374671 13194139535924 true] [17592186374667 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045451 13194139535924 true] [17592186374667 1041 "field-1" 13194139535924 true] [17592186374667 1104 #edb/ref 17592186374670 13194139535924 true] [17592186374667 1110 #uuid "2189c44e-c6fc-5459-91e4-e02ae31ddba1" 13194139535924 true] [17592186374668 1034 "\\frac{{n}^{2}}{8}" 13194139535924 true] [17592186374668 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535924 true] [17592186374668 1111 #uuid "c02d751b-6dc1-58c4-9827-6697a10da147" 13194139535924 true] [17592186374669 1034 "\\frac{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{4}" 13194139535924 true] [17592186374669 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535924 true] [17592186374669 1111 #uuid "cc981746-8442-5899-8593-7c7c903d75bf" 13194139535924 true] [17592186374670 1034 "\\frac{{n}^{2}}{16}" 13194139535924 true] [175